# Exercise Pages (Not Lessons)

Coding exercises are separate from lessons. Follow these rules so pages match the Tufte lesson theme.

## Naming & labels

- Call them **Exercise** / **Ex** — never "Lesson" in title, tray, or dashboard.
- Say it **once** in `<p class="meta">` (e.g. `Capstone exercise &bull; Module 02`).
- **No redundant badges** like "Exercise · Not a Lesson" above the title.

## Visual theme (mandatory)

- Link `../assets/lesson.css` from `exercises/*.html`.
- **Reuse lesson design tokens** — never invent a dark/alternate palette:
  - `var(--text)`, `var(--muted)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--bg)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--surface)`
- **Buttons** match `.quiz-options button` in `lesson.css`:
  - `var(--btn-bg)` / `var(--text)` / `1px solid var(--border)`; hover `var(--btn-hover)` + accent border
  - Never hardcode `#fff` / `#fafaf5` — breaks dark theme
- **Tables**: `border: 1px solid var(--border)`; header `background: var(--surface)`
- **Forbidden**: ad-hoc dark colors (`#0f172a`, `#334155`, `#1e293b`, blue badge chips, etc.)

## File layout

- HTML: `exercises/<module>-<name>-exercise.html`
- Java stub: `exercises/<Name>Exercise.java` (single copy-paste file, JUnit 5, JavaDoc scenarios + tests)

## Indexing (same discipline as lessons)

1. **`index.html`** — drawer entry with `Ex` number, meta `Coding` not `min read`; counts `X Lessons &bull; Y Exercise`
2. **`lesson-tray.js`** — `{ kind: 'exercise', num: 'Ex', file: '...-exercise.html', ... }`; tray uses `../exercises/` from lessons
3. **Nav chain** — last lesson `➡️ Next: … Exercise`; exercise page `⬅️ Prev: …` + Home
4. **Search index** — `python scripts/build-lesson-search-index.py` (after tray entry exists)

## Checklist

- [ ] Uses `lesson.css` variables only (no off-theme colors)
- [ ] No duplicate exercise badge if meta already says exercise
- [ ] Indexed in dashboard + lesson-tray with `kind: 'exercise'`
- [ ] Prev/next nav wired from last lesson
- [ ] `lesson-search-index.json` rebuilt via build script

